<http://rs.tdwg.org/chrono/terms/ChronometricAge> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "`An age range associated with a specimen derived from an AMS dating assay applied to an oyster shell in the same stratum`; `An age range associated with a specimen derived from a ceramics analysis based on other materials found in the same stratum`; `A maximum age associated with a specimen derived from K-Ar dating applied to a proximal volcanic tuff found stratigraphically below the specimen`; `An age range of a specimen based on its biostratigraphic context`; `An age of a specimen based on what is reported in legacy collections data`."@en .
